  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195146/assets/473b8a18bb4d2bf77cfe18eb735bcb64ec95a551faadb18ad38f561c81d3b99c.png)\n\nFind the area of the rectangle $ABCD$ shown above.",
  "worked_solution": "The area of a rectangle is given by \n\n$$\nA=a\\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that \n\n$$\na=AB=9\\,cm,\\,b=AD=5\\,cm.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the area of the rectangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =a\\cdot b=9\\cdot 5=45\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
